  "instance_name": "littering_fine",
  "label": "Littering Fine as a Social Punishment",
  "description": "The concept of a fine for littering is a real-world legal and social consequence. The meme uses this as a punchline to exaggerate the absurdity of a parent’s minor infraction. Understanding that littering fines are common and enforced by municipalities is necessary to appreciate the joke’s setup — it’s not a major crime, making the implication of a fine for a parent’s behavior more humorous and ironic.",
